{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880475-using-wraiths-and-their-lands-in-other-games-many-questions","id":880475,"title":"Using Wraiths and their lands in other games- many questions.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-02T14:30:55-07:00","id":880475,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Using Wraiths and their lands in other games- many questions.","content":"So I had the idea to use the dark umbra in werewolf, and in a one on one session of vampire we've got a player being a Giovanni (specifically a milliner) in anarch territory. I don't have wraith, but I quite like putting everything in the one-world. I don't particularly like using the minimal translations found in the books (IE spectres use obtenebration) and, whilst I certainly like to use my imagination, I really do like sending HIT marks after claith and citing the rules when they call me on my nonsense.<br /> <br /> I'm told that sometimes, supernaturals go on to become wraiths. How does that work? Do they hold on to any of their former powers? Can garou shift or use gifts? Do Cainites keep disciplines? Do nosferatu return to their mortal seeming and gangrel loose their features? Do changelings remember anything?<br /> <br /> what happens to the body on a trip to the shadowlands? for all of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> I took some interest in the Giovanni section of the Lore of the Clans book. I was just wondering how easy is it to add to the spirit slaves backround, and what the manifest ability means. Like will Mr Tom appear behind baddy No 4 and engage in fisticuffs, or is the wraith way of doing things different?<br /> <br /> <br /> My story hook for the necromancer right now is as follows<br /> Gangrel asked the player to summon a person for him.<br /> The summon failed despite a successful roll, meaning either diablorie or still living. (or golconda, but these folks know nothing of that)<br /> Gangrel asks the player to summon another person, who'll know where this person is.<br /> That other person appears, is the Gangrel's 'sister' who he killed, and the person they're looking for is the resting sire of the two.<br /> The sister wants her brother to fail and promises a period of servitude to the necromancer should the player assist in that, the brother is offering significant rewards too.<br /> <br /> Now my questions are<br /> Will the sister have gangrel features (as well as signs of arcanoi, which include embody, but no means of possession, the player will have to do that for her)<br /> Will she have vampiric powers?<br /> Would she have gangrel powers were she to embody?<br /> Whatabout animal features that are useful?<br /> If she was unusualy powerful due to gen, would that cross over into her wraithly self (IE does 6 intelligence alive mean 6 intelligence dead?)<br /> Will she be able to tutor in disciplines?<br /> <br /> That said, not all people come back as wraiths... But I don't even know how ghosts are sometimes haunting places and othertimes in a different realm...<br /> <br /> <b>As I did a skim over the wraith book, I noticed something really significant </b><br /> -Most individuals don't become wraiths and either transcend or meet oblivion... so can you still summon them?<br /> -A great deal of wraiths get transformed into something else. Timmy the barber you tried to summon might show up as a rifle, a pair of shoes or a brick that might be an important part of a structure. You might accidentally get a specter, or something really out there like a barghest or cerement or some other deep horror. Timmy could be anything. So, If i wanted answers from timmy and he's really been a hairbrush all this time... what happens?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T04:10:26-07:00","id":880862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880475-using-wraiths-and-their-lands-in-other-games-many-questions#post880475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>As I did a skim over the wraith book, I noticed something really significant </b></div> </div> </div> </div>Based on your questions, I think reading the book would be a very good idea:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -Most individuals don't become wraiths and either transcend or meet oblivion... so can you still summon them? </div> </div> </div>No<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -A great deal of wraiths get transformed into something else. Timmy the barber you tried to summon might show up as a rifle, a pair of shoes or a brick that might be an important part of a structure. You might accidentally get a specter, or something really out there like a barghest or cerement or some other deep horror. Timmy could be anything. So, If i wanted answers from timmy and he's really been a hairbrush all this time... what happens? </div> </div> </div>You're probably out of luck.<br /> <br /> Soulforging or permanently Moliating a wraith into an object is a one-way street, and pretty much destroys the mind of the wraith in question. Some masters of Phantasm (an Arcanoi that interacts with dreams) have had some luck, reaching into the fevered dreams of soulforged items to retrieve information from (what's left of) their mind . . . but that's about it. Once you've been turned into an ashtray, you're staying an ashtray. And ashtrays aren't exactly great conversationalists <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A Specter is a wraith that's lost control of their dark side (i.e. their Shadow), and which now conspires against . . . pretty much everything else in existence. Many go so far as to outright worship the forces of Oblivion. You can summon one, but skimping on your defensive protocols is a very, very bad idea. Trusting anything they say isn't exactly wise, either.<br /> <br /> A barghest (<i>et al</i>) has had their higher mental functions gutted, to the point that they're little more than animals. Again, not great for conversation, but they might be able to communicate a few things (growling at an enemy, pulling you towards a clue they've noticed). If something is too complicated for a dog to communicate, a barghest probably can't, either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, not all people come back as wraiths... But I don't even know how ghosts are sometimes haunting places and othertimes in a different realm... </div> </div> </div>The best analogy is probably from <b>Werewolf: the Apocalypse</b>. Sometimes a werewolf is on Earth, and sometimes they're exploring the spirit worlds of the Umbra. Similarly, sometimes a wraith is haunting Earth, and sometimes they're travelling in the depths of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm told that sometimes, supernaturals go on to become wraiths. How does that work? Do they hold on to any of their former powers? Can garou shift or use gifts? Do Cainites keep disciplines? Do nosferatu return to their mortal seeming and gangrel loose their features? Do changelings remember anything?<br /> <br /> what happens to the body on a trip to the shadowlands? for all of them. </div> </div> </div>For a supernatural to become a wraith is very rare - and pretty much subject to Storyteller fiat. Off-hand, I can name one one canon example: Samuel Haight. And he was the exception to many, many rules<br /> <br /> A number of supernatural creatures have their own &quot;version&quot; of wraithdom, though. Some fae become banshees, a mummy's ba could easily be mistaken for a wraith, a mage with the right Spheres can do pretty much anything they want . . . And others have powers that let them visit the Underworld (a.k.a the Dark Umbra): Silent Striders, kuei-jin, some Cainites . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 05-03-2016, 07:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T05:16:30-07:00","id":880882,"title":"","content":"Ah, Ok. I looked at rules again for necromancy. Summoning a ghost that's been destroyed leads to you feeling the underworld but not getting the guy. <br /> <br /> ok. So you can accidently summon barghests (and maybe other things)<br /> <br /> <br /> From supernaturals turning into wraiths...<br /> Most Garou end up on the colourful side of things, but a few don't for a few nasty reasons. Did read something about the last howler who died going on his own crusade there. <br /> As for the other supernaturals... well... ah.. They've got huge willpower. There does seem to be the implication that vampires can be found on the other side. (or at least you get confirmation that they passed through)<br /> Cathayans are very much like risen. So if they die...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T05:29:59-07:00","id":880889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880475-using-wraiths-and-their-lands-in-other-games-many-questions?p=880882#post880882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(. . .)Cathayans are very much like risen. So if they die...</div> </div> </div> </div>They go back to Hell (i.e. Yomi). &quot;Cathayan&quot; is an old Cainite term for the kuei-jin. And while they're able to visit the Underworld (Bone Flowers do so regularly), they're very different. This is their last shot at avoiding eternal damnation, and their time in Hell has damaged their connection to the rest of reality. There are some anecdotal examples of Thrashing Dragon kuei-jin becoming yulan-jin (body-hopping minor splat) when their real body is destroyed. . . but that's not the same thing as a wraith.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: Of course, you're free to house-rule anything you want, but the canon material is pretty clear on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T05:34:30-07:00","id":880891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880475-using-wraiths-and-their-lands-in-other-games-many-questions?p=880882#post880882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cathayans are very much like risen. So if they die...</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not really. Because if a Cathayan dies a final death, his spirit goes back to Hell, into the waiting hands of the monsters it escaped from. Most likely to be personaly tormentedfor his audacity and resistance against Yomi...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T06:05:47-07:00","id":880912,"title":"","content":"So, Any ideas on supernaturals becoming wraiths? Especially vampires and werewolves, though the other stuff is interesting. <br /> <br /> To my knowledge wraith items don't leave their realm, right? No stygian steel or otherwordly lanterns, yeah? <br /> <br /> Will Conjuring wraiths get players involved in wraith politics (ah, My servitor has an arcanoi that they shouldn't, The hierarchy are demanding I release her to them) <br /> How bad are spectres? Like other than dopplegangers I'm guessing black spiral bad. <br /> How bad are shadows to the player? <br /> Do non-wraiths see the visible signs of arcanoi? <br /> <br /> (also, what's the difference between embody 4 and 5. Like 5 just seems to be more effort to do but a bit more enjoyable.) <br /> <br /> Also, it seems really, really easy for wraiths to mess with supernaturals. shroud is -2 difficulty around them? Did necromancers just become all powerful?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T09:43:28-07:00","id":881052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/880475-using-wraiths-and-their-lands-in-other-games-many-questions?p=880912#post880912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, it seems really, really easy for wraiths to mess with supernaturals. shroud is -2 difficulty around them? Did necromancers just become all powerful?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Not at all. There are MANY threads on this subject on the Wraith board. A few are even currently ongoing. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T12:17:20-07:00","id":883095,"title":"","content":"The thing you may not see is that the metaphysics of the Underworld keeps most ghosts from ever interacting with our world, and for those same reasons it keeps mortal (or undead) necromancers from reaching most wraiths. Only those restless souls closest to our world can be called here via any magics. It works (in very simplified terms, including terms that you may or may not want to remember in case there is a quiz) like this:<br /> <br /> The <b>Shadowlands</b> is the very near deadlands that are a reflection of our world, separated by the <b>Shroud</b>, a wall of (dis)belief that keeps the two separate. A wraith on the Shadowlands side may see into our world, the <b>Skinlands</b> as it is called by many wraiths, and with the correct powers can interact with the Skinlands for a brief time. On the opposite side, a necromancer of any stripe can only reach into the Shadowlands to summon ghosts or wander about (with, say, the Necromancy Ash Path)... Okay, there ARE some exceptions, but figure that ghosts that are gonna be summoned and/or fuck with the our world are in the Shadowlands. However, as close are they are, it's not a simple thing for them to actually STAY close. Wraiths stay near our world only because of connexions left this world after death, what are known as <b>fetters</b> that bind a wraith to this world. A fetter can be a person, an object, a place, really anything that is part of the ghost's unfinished business in our world. Oh yeah, knowing and holding a ghost's fetter can be a HUGE help for a necromancer to influence any wraith. The thing is, as a wraith ages or grows in power, fetters are lost in various ways. Once all of a ghost's fetters are gone, she cannot stay in the Shadowlands. Again, there ARE examples of this being something other than a hard-and-fast rule, but let's not linger here as we've the next layer of the Underworld to consider.<br /> <br /> Below the Shadowlands is the <b>Tempest</b> (also called the Sea of Shadows, the Sunless Sea, and other, regional terms) where the oldest ghosts exist in realms that are equal parts a stormy ocean of memory and hurricanes of emotions. Here is where ghostly political organisations are found for the most part, residing on 'islands' in the Tempest, and here ghosts fight and vie in ways that are far, far removed from our world. The greatest of these ghost nations (at least for the Western dead) is <b>Stygia</b>, seat of the Dark Kingdom of Iron, located on the Isle of Sorrows. Here the great dictator Charon set up a government of the dead, and the most important document of his regime is the <b>Dictum Mortuum</b>, a set of inviolable (only if one gets caught) laws of how the restless dead may interact with the living, and the monolithic political engine that is Stygia takes these things VERY seriously... Unless they don't, but that's ANOTHER exception that we're gonna gloss over here.<br /> <br /> ...So all of that boils down to (way, way simplified):<br /> <br /> <b>1.</b> Not all ghosts are reachable by necromancers.<br /> <b>2.</b> Those who are still remain bound by metaphysical limitations.<br /> <b>3.</b> The ghost hierarchy (known as <b>The Hierarchy</b>, conveniently enough) makes it difficult for ghosts, much less powerful ghosts, to cause problems on our side of the Shroud.<br /> <b>4.</b> The scariest ghosts are too far away to really interact with our world, and they're disinclined to find our world worth the worry.<br /> <br /> Then there's all of the mystical powers of the Arcanoi, the balancing factor the Shadow and spectres, the fuel of Pathos and anti-fuel of Angst, innate ghostly abilities of perception and shapes and their needs to nurture driving forces (i.e. their Passions)... none of which QUITE match what's in the various other game lines of the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> It's a difficult thing to really, truly bring <b>Wraith: the Oblivion</b> into any other game line, I find, but it's ALSO hard to keep it from seeping into the other games. There are wonderful overlaps to <b>Vampire</b> via Clan Giovanni and other bloodlines, to <b>Werewolf</b> after Revised Edition, to <b>Mage</b> since forever with the Chakravanti/Euthanatos, and even <b>Changeling</b> and <b>Demon</b> had huge crossover potential. That state of affairs makes a 'faithful' crossover look quite desirable in theory, but the amount of nuance and specificity found in <b>Wraith</b> makes such very, very difficult in practice. I do hold hope that <b>Wraith 20th Anniversary</b> will make things easier, but as it stands, <b>Wraith</b> is challenging to use as written in any other game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T21:38:55-07:00","id":930711,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm wrong but as an example didn't 50 capadocians end up going to the underworld in death and then finding a way back to earth as the Harbingers?<br /> <br /> Maybe in their centuries of solitude and inprisonment they discovered a way to guarantee a vampire goes to the underworld when they die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3837-slimjimjohnson","name":"Slimjimjohnson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T23:46:58-07:00","id":930736,"title":"","content":"If a supernatural becomes a Wraith, they are a NORMAL Wraith for all intents and purposes.<br /> <br /> A Nosferatu will probaly KEEP his ugly appearance as thats how he percieves himself, but can go through Extensive Moliation to take a more pleasing appearance.<br /> <br /> Similarly some Garou ghosts, take Crinos or lupus form based on self Image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T21:51:57-07:00","id":931811,"title":"","content":"Frankly, supernatural ghosts are sort of gimmicky, and sometimes being 'special' during your earthly existence might prove detrimental. Imagine that you were a werewolf that died and somehow escaped Gaia's embrace... your former Garou nature doesn't give you powers in Shadowlands, and if anything, it might cause your darker side to be very, very powerful: emotional echoes of a life full of rage combined with the knowledge that you are a Wyrm-horror cannot be healthy for a psyche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}